Buong configuration

Kung gusto mong copy-paste, ito ang pinakaimportanteng portion:

enable
configure terminal

!
! =========================
! WAN INTERFACE
! =========================
interface TenGigabitEthernet1/0/2
 description WAN_TO_ISP
 no switchport
 ip address 193.168.2.10 255.255.255.0
 ip nat outside
 no shutdown
 exit

!
! =========================
! LAN GATEWAY
! =========================
interface Vlan20
 description LAN_GATEWAY
 ip address 194.168.2.1 255.255.255.0
 ip nat inside
 no shutdown
 exit

!
! =========================
! NAT ACL
! =========================
access-list 1 permit 194.168.2.0 0.0.0.255

!
! =========================
! NAT/PAT
! =========================
ip nat inside source list 1 interface TenGigabitEthernet1/0/2 overload

!
! =========================
! DEFAULT ROUTE
! =========================
ip route 0.0.0.0 0.0.0.0 193.168.2.1

end
write memory
Pero may isang bagay tayong kailangang tanggalin/ayusin

Currently ginagamit mo ang VLAN10 bilang WAN:

VLAN10 = 193.168.2.0/24

at mayroon kang:

Vlan10
ip address 193.168.2.10

At may DHCP pool ka rin na:

Pool WAN
193.168.2.0/24
default-router 193.168.2.1

Hindi ko irerekomendang gamitin ang DHCP pool na WAN sa final design natin kung ang WAN ay direct physical connection mula CoreSwitch papunta sa ISP router.

Pwede nating alisin:

no ip dhcp pool WAN

At eventually alisin din natin ang VLAN10 kung wala na talaga itong purpose.

Step 6 — Importanteng test

Pagkatapos ng configuration:

1. Check WAN
show ip interface brief

Dapat makita:

Te1/0/2    193.168.2.10    YES    NVRAM    up    up
Vlan20     194.168.2.1     YES    NVRAM    up    up
2. Test ISP gateway

Sa CoreSwitch:

ping 193.168.2.1

Dapat successful muna ito.

Kung hindi successful, huwag muna nating isipin ang NAT.

3. Test Internet mismo
ping 8.8.8.8

Kung successful:

CoreSwitch → ISP → Internet

working na ang routing.

4. Check routing table
show ip route

Dapat mayroon kang:

S* 0.0.0.0/0 [1/0] via 193.168.2.1

Ang S* ay static default route.

5. Test from PC

PC should receive something like:

IP Address      194.168.2.101
Subnet Mask     255.255.255.0
Default Gateway 194.168.2.1
DNS             8.8.8.8

Then:

ping 194.168.2.1

then:

ping 193.168.2.1

then:

ping 8.8.8.8

then:

ping google.com
Step 7 — Check NAT

Ito ang pinakaimportanteng command:

show ip nat translations

Kapag nag-ping ka mula sa PC papuntang 8.8.8.8, dapat magkaroon ng entries.

Pwede rin:

show ip nat statistics

Makikita mo kung may NAT translations at counters.

Isang importanteng distinction

May dalawang possible setup tayo:

Setup A — CoreSwitch directly connected to ISP router
Internet
   |
ISP Router
   |
Te1/0/2
CoreSwitch
   |
L2 Switch
   |
Clients

Ito ang recommended ko para sa lab mo.

CoreSwitch ang:

DHCP Server
Default Gateway
Inter-VLAN Router
Internet Router
NAT/PAT Router
Setup B — May existing FortiGate/router between CoreSwitch and Internet
Internet
   |
FortiGate/Router
   |
CoreSwitch
   |
L2 Switch
   |
Clients

Sa ganitong setup, hindi kailangan ng NAT sa CoreSwitch dahil ang FortiGate/router ang dapat gumawa ng NAT. CoreSwitch simply needs a default route pointing to the FortiGate.

Sa config mo ngayon

Dahil mayroon kang 193.168.2.1 bilang WAN gateway at 194.168.2.1 bilang LAN gateway, mukhang nagse-set up ka ng simulated ISP/WAN network. Kaya puwede nating ituloy exactly along this design.

Ang next step ko sa'yo ay huwag muna nating galawin ang L2 switch. I-configure muna natin ang CoreSwitch WAN + NAT + default route, tapos i-test natin bawat hop:

Core → ISP → Internet → NAT → PC.

Kung gusto mo, pwede kitang bigyan ng isang final clean configuration ng buong CoreSwitch + L2 Switch, kasama ang tamang VLAN10/WAN at VLAN20/LAN design, para copy-paste na lang at walang conflict sa existing config mo.
